      'Retrieves the GLQL schema: data sources with their filter, display and sort fields, the operator, value kind and reference type vocabularies, the available functions, and the display types a query can be rendered as. The document describes the query language. A query against a data source that is not available to the user fails at `POST /glql`. The document changes only when GitLab is upgraded. It is served with an `ETag`, so clients can send `If-None-Match` to revalidate and receive `304 Not Modified` instead of the full document. The endpoint takes no parameters and returns the same document for every user. Analytics modes list the arguments their dimensions and metrics accept in `parameterized_fields`, so a query can set them explicitly rather than relying on the default. Each entry has a `name` and a `parameters` array. Each parameter has a `name` and a `kind`, and can have `values`, `min`, `max`, `min_days`, `max_days`, `default`, `optional`, `required`, `requires`, `items`, `min_length`, `max_length`, and `strictly_ascending`. This feature was introduced in GitLab 19.3.',
